NOTES=["Vertical map: 180 m from the rim floor to the vault; the plan view is stacked, so the cross-section in the image is the real layout. Every zone below the rim has at least one overlook onto the abyss on its west side.",
"The Rim: 800 m across; the hatch at the centre; bone stakes at r=350 m mark the worm's line. Beyond the stakes the sand shakes for 8 s, then the worm consumes the diver (no down). The worm is visible tunneling at r=450-600 at all times: a horizon feature, nothing more.",
"Training loop (station): Mess -> caiman corridor -> Labs -> pressure door -> Reactor -> service shaft (one-way back up to the Mess). About 2 min, indoors, past the seal, the caiman, and the vent trap.",
"Training loop (deep): Galleries -> Warrens -> Airlock A -> Mess -> Reactor -> Vault -> vault stair back -> Reactor -> Labs -> Airlock B -> Warrens -> Galleries. About 6 min; the only loop that touches both Lockers.",
"Blood flow: almost none. The water barely moves, so blood pools where it's made (decay 0.5% base here, not 2%); the only currents are the reactor's warm plume (rises from the Reactor up the service shaft into the Mess) and the brine pool's drain over Overlook 3.",
"Sightlines: rim unlimited but dark (lamp 25 m); galleries 20 m; warrens 8 m; station 10-15 m; vault 40 m. Alarm regions: Rim, Galleries and Warrens, Station, Vault; the Remnant enters at the two airlocks and the upper airlock.",
"Specimens: salamanders breed +1 per 90 s per pair in the bunks and coelacanths +1 per 120 s per pair in the wet lab (cap 12 each); only the caiman eats them. An overrun station is loud and full of blood whenever a Remnant squad passes through."]
BOSS=["The Lantern Leviathan — an anglerfish the size of the reactor. Arena: the Lowest Vault until tide 12; after that its lure appears anywhere in the galleries, warrens, and station (it swims the tubes), so the whole descent is the arena.",
"HP 15,000 (x1.08 per tide); armor: its body is dark and hard to see (hits on the body do 50%); weak point: the gills behind the lure, exposed for 2 s after every Swallow and for 5 s when the lure is shot out (500 damage to the lure).",
"Phase 1 (100-60%): Lure (an emergency light appears where none was; curious beasts and divers drift to it), Swallow (a diver taken whole: teammates have 5 s to deal 200 to the gills), Bite. It stays in the black coral.",
"Phase 2 (60-30%): Dark (every light in 30 m goes out for 6 s: lamps, kelp, beacons; only its lure remains), and it moves through the vault's coral like a shark through kelp; sixgills follow the blood it makes.",
"Phase 3 (30-0%): the lure splits into three (two are decoys that Swallow nothing but hold a diver 2 s); it drops the collapsing ledge if a diver stands on Overlook 5; the Relict may arrive for the corpses and fight it (the Relict wins one time in three).",
"Arena rules: shooting out the lure blinds it 5 s; the reactor vent scalds it for 10% if it's lured into the Reactor hall (Beacon 4); black coral can be shot down to open sightlines (loud); Widow's Ink and Cold Coffin are sold in its own vault for a reason.",
"Kill reward: 1,500 base scrip x tide, a Locker weapon each, and the station's master key (opens tank 7: the Relict egg, which starts the Abyssal Lure quest). It reforms in the vault after 6 minutes at 50% HP."]
FACTION=dict(name="The Remnant",intro="What's left of the research station: mad researchers in pressure suits, clockwork sentinels that leak oil instead of blood, and void cultists who want to reach the edge. Sentinels have no scent; researchers and cultists bleed normally and are eaten; the Station Chief's mech is size 5 and the Relict attacks it on sight.",
units=[("Sentinel",250,"Rotary needler","20 x 900 rpm in 3 s bursts","Slow (1.0); walks on the floor","Holds chokepoints and doorways; never advances; spins up for 1 s","A rising whine and a red lamp","Rotary needler (a Locker-class weapon, 60 rounds), 300"),
("Researcher",120,"Gas grenades and a repair torch","Gas: 15/s in a 4 m cloud for 6 s; the torch heals Sentinels 20/s","Diver speed","Stays behind the Sentinels; deploys and re-aims lure beacons","A hiss before a throw; the torch's blue flame","Gas grenades (tactical x2), a beacon key, 240"),
("Void Cultist",130,"Ritual knife","30 melee; chants: divers within 10 m lose 5 nerves/s and drift 0.3 m/s toward the nearest overlook","Diver speed","Tries to reach an overlook edge; on reaching it, summons 3 hatchetfish swarms and a Colossal Squid tentacle for 20 s","Arms wide, walking backward toward the edge","A void charm, 220"),
("Station Chief (Hunts)",1200,"Diving mech: twin harpoon cannons and a grab-claw","Cannon 200 per bolt (1 per 4 s); claw hold 3 s then 120","Slow (1.2); size 5","Anchors the Hunt from the mech bay; switches Beacon 4 on; the Relict attacks it on sight","Floodlights sweep before the cannons fire; hydraulic hiss before the claw","The Stormlock rack unlocks; mech parts (build), 800")],
tactics=["Squads enter at Airlock A, Airlock B, or the upper airlock; Sentinels take the nearest doorway and hold it; Researchers set a lure beacon toward the divers; Cultists walk for the nearest overlook.",
"On contact: Sentinels spin up and hold; Researchers gas the corridor the divers are in and heal the Sentinels; the Cultist's chant drifts divers toward the edge. Break a Sentinel with a limpet or flank it (its needler has a 90-degree arc).",
"Sentinels are immune to scent and blood rules and ignore beasts; Researchers and Cultists are eaten like anyone and run from goblin sharks and the caiman.",
"Chum and ink do nothing to Sentinels; the reactor vent and the pressure door kill them; the pen doors trap the caiman away from them (they know) or onto them (a build).",
"In a Hunt the Chief holds the mech bay and turns Beacon 4 on (drawing beasts to the Forge); leading the mech to Overlook 5 brings the Relict, which ends the Hunt one way or the other."],
barks=["Sentinel: (klaxon) 'Perimeter. Perimeter.'","Researcher: 'Specimens in the hall. Tag them.' / 'Beacon set. Let the deep collect them.'","Cultist: 'The edge is a door.' / 'Walk with me to the light below.'","Researcher losing: 'Fall back to the reactor. The Chief has it.'","Chief: 'Nobody leaves the station. Nobody ever has.' / 'Floodlights. Harpoons. Bring me the samples.'","Chief sees the Relict: 'No... the egg. It came back for the egg.'"])
